                "style": "Poetic ethnography, sweeping natural landscapes, staged 'authentic' moments, and a focus on man's struggle against nature.",
                "techniques": [
                    "Salvage Ethnography: Attempted to document traditional cultures before they vanished, though he often forced subjects to enact abandoned, anachronistic practices for the camera.",
                    "Narrative Imposition: Applied Hollywood-style narrative arcs (hero vs. nature) to raw, unscripted footage to make ethnographic reality compelling for mass audiences.",
                    "Intimate Observation: Lived with his subjects for years before filming, building a deep, familial trust that translated into incredibly intimate, naturalistic portraits."
                ],
                "lessons": [
                    "Find the narrative in the real. Reality is chaotic; the documentary filmmaker's job is to carve a compelling, emotional story out of raw existence.",
                    "Question documentary truth. Understand that the moment you point a camera at someone, or ask them to repeat an action, you are altering reality."
                ],
