        "description": "<strong>Alfred Hitchcock</strong><br><em style='color: var(--accent-gold); display: block; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 0; font-size: 1.1rem;'>“To make a great film, you need three things: the script, the script, and the script.”</em>The screenwriter designs the blueprint of the film. Writing for cinema is the art of externalizing internal struggles, structuring pacing across acts, and writing dialogue where what is *not* said is more important than what is.",
