                "plot": "In the Los Angeles criminal underworld, several stories interweave in a non-chronological mosaic. Philosophical hitmen Vincent Vega (John Travolta) and Jules Winnfield (Samuel L. Jackson) handle business for crime lord Marsellus Wallace while debating the nature of foot massages and divine intervention. Vincent is tasked with entertaining Marsellus's dangerous wife Mia (Uma Thurman), a night that spirals into crisis. Aging boxer Butch Coolidge (Bruce Willis) takes Marsellus's money to throw a fight, then wins it — setting off a chain of bloody consequences. And a pair of small-time diner robbers plan an audacious mid-breakfast heist. Through unexpected detours, sudden violence, dark comedy, and razor-sharp dialogue, the film explores fate, redemption, and the bizarre rhythms of life on the margins."
